   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Indirect questions with «si»",
     "texto": [
      "For yes-or-no questions **si** is used: **Il demande si tu viens** (he asks if you are coming).",
      "If the main verb is in the past: **Il a demandé si tu venais** (he asked if you were coming)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Questions with what, where, when",
     "texto": [
      "The question word is used: **Il demande ce que tu fais** (he asks what you are doing), **Il a demandé où nous habitions** (he asked where we lived), **Il demande quand le train part** (he asks when the train leaves)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Time and place words",
     "texto": [
      "When reporting from another moment, some markers change: **demain** can become **le lendemain**, **aujourd'hui** becomes **ce jour-là** and **ici** becomes **là**.",
      "The change depends on who is reporting and when."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
